{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734694",
      "title": "The Special \"children\" Prop",
      "sourceHash": "a7d1589b6383b0d1026c654246f3525c7bca87c61220cbd3393d5194bd78cecd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "Let's continue diving deeper into React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "We get this form here, this input form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 9.9,
          "en": "and it looks decent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.9,
          "end": 13.98,
          "en": "but I'd like to open it as a modal overlay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.98,
          "end": 17.01,
          "en": "So some overlay that's above the rest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.01,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "of the content on this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 24.123,
          "en": "And in the end, achieving this look is a pure CSS thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 26.85,
          "en": "Now, what we could do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.85,
          "end": 30.93,
          "en": "is we could edit the styles of this NewPost component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.93,
          "end": 33.75,
          "en": "such that it has this modal look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.75,
          "end": 36.66,
          "en": "You can add a backdrop behind the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.66,
          "end": 39.933,
          "en": "so some background so that it looks like an overlay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.83,
          "end": 43.323,
          "en": "But I'd rather take a different route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.22,
          "end": 45.72,
          "en": "In the end, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "that in the place where I use this NewPost component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 52.14,
          "en": "and I just pressed the auto format shortcut here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.14,
          "end": 55.05,
          "en": "to put these props into separate lines,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.05,
          "end": 58.14,
          "en": "which is still valid code but easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.14,
          "end": 59.79,
          "en": "But I'd like to take a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.79,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "where I have a new Modal component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 63.78,
          "en": "which doesn't exist yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 66.36,
          "en": "which can be wrapped around NewPost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.36,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "to give that NewPost that modal overlay look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 72.21000000000001,
          "en": "Again, this Modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.21000000000001,
          "end": 74.16,
          "en": "is a component we have yet to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.16,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "but I'd like to have a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 77.763,
          "en": "that can be used like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.93,
          "end": 80.46000000000001,
          "en": "Now, the idea behind that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.46000000000001,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "is simply that on more complex websites,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 86.67,
          "en": "chances are high that you have all kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.67,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "of content that should have that overlay look,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 93.12,
          "en": "not just this NewPost form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.12,
          "end": 96.363,
          "en": "but maybe also some warning dialogs, anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.77000000000001,
          "end": 99.72,
          "en": "So it would be nice to have such a wrapper,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.72,
          "end": 103.41,
          "en": "and being able to wrap content with components of yours",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.41,
          "end": 107.31,
          "en": "is indeed another core React concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.31,
          "end": 110.19,
          "en": "You can really only compose flexible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.19,
          "end": 112.41,
          "en": "powerful user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 115.11,
          "en": "if you're able to also wrap components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.11,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "with other components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 120.69,
          "en": "to apply some extra styles to them, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.69,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "And therefore, to achieve this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "I'll add a new component called Modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 128.79,
          "en": "A Modal.jsx file is therefore added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.79,
          "end": 133.05,
          "en": "And attached, you find a link to a Modal.module.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.05,
          "end": 136.35,
          "en": "which you should add, which simply comes with some styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.35,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "that will help us achieve that overlay look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 143.67000000000002,
          "en": "And then inside of Modal.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.67000000000002,
          "end": 146.32,
          "en": "we can create a Modal function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.27,
          "end": 149.853,
          "en": "and export that as a default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.78,
          "end": 154.71,
          "en": "And then in there, I wanna return a fragment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.71,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "so this empty tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 161.31,
          "en": "where I have a div without any content inside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.31,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "And then a dialog element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 165.69,
          "en": "that will hold the actual modal content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.69,
          "end": 169.5,
          "en": "and this div will be used to render a background,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.5,
          "end": 173.493,
          "en": "a backdrop as it's also often called for this modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 178.68,
          "en": "Now, we should import some CSS classes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.68,
          "end": 183.68,
          "en": "from Modal.module.css.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.93,
          "end": 187.11,
          "en": "And then assign one class here to this div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.11,
          "end": 190.713,
          "en": "and that would be the backdrop class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.18,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "And to the dialog, we should also add a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.3,
          "end": 197.973,
          "en": "and that's the modal class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.99,
          "end": 202.86,
          "en": "And backdrop and modal are both CSS classes defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.86,
          "end": 204.933,
          "en": "in this CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.22,
          "end": 208.11,
          "en": "Now with that, we have a Modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.11,
          "end": 212.34,
          "en": "but if we try to use it as a wrapper around NewPost,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.34,
          "end": 213.9,
          "en": "so inside of PostsList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.9,
          "end": 218.9,
          "en": "if I go there and I then try to import this Modal component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 226.52,
          "en": "which we just added from ./Modal, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.82999999999998,
          "end": 229.17000000000002,
          "en": "and I then use it as a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.17000000000002,
          "end": 232.98,
          "en": "with the opening and closing tag around NewPost,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.98,
          "end": 237.51,
          "en": "you will see that it doesn't really look the way it should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.51,
          "end": 239.64,
          "en": "It looks the backdrop is visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.64,
          "end": 242.07,
          "en": "We have this gray background,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.07,
          "end": 245.79,
          "en": "this transparent black background everywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.79,
          "end": 249.063,
          "en": "but the form and the modal is nowhere to be seen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.89,
          "end": 254.64,
          "en": "The reason for that is that if you wrap content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.64,
          "end": 255.99,
          "en": "no matter if it's a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.99,
          "end": 258.36,
          "en": "or some default built-in elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.36,
          "end": 261.81,
          "en": "if you wrap content with another custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 261.81,
          "end": 264.21,
          "en": "by default, React does not know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.21,
          "end": 266.79,
          "en": "where to put that wrapped content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.79,
          "end": 269.04,
          "en": "inside the wrapping component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.04,
          "end": 271.713,
          "en": "So inside the Modal component in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.64,
          "end": 274.44,
          "en": "You have to tell React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.44,
          "end": 276.993,
          "en": "where that wrapped content should go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.95,
          "end": 281.61,
          "en": "And you do tell React with another special prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 281.61,
          "end": 283.68,
          "en": "So with the props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.68,
          "end": 288.65999999999997,
          "en": "And that special prop is the children prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.85,
          "end": 294.03,
          "en": "By the way, instead of always using props dot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.03,
          "end": 297.03,
          "en": "you can also use object destructuring here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.03,
          "end": 300.39,
          "en": "to directly get access to a specific value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.39,
          "end": 304.023,
          "en": "So to a specific property of that props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 305.28,
          "end": 307.11,
          "en": "This is not only possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.11,
          "end": 309.63,
          "en": "when using this special children prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.63,
          "end": 311.76,
          "en": "but it works with all props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 311.76,
          "end": 313.62,
          "en": "So for the Post component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.62,
          "end": 316.95,
          "en": "you could, for example, also use object destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 316.95,
          "end": 319.17,
          "en": "to get the author and the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 319.17,
          "end": 323.793,
          "en": "and then save yourself the props dot call down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 325.29,
          "end": 326.7,
          "en": "But that's just a side note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 326.7,
          "end": 329.58,
          "en": "So this is just a more concise way of getting access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 329.58,
          "end": 330.72,
          "en": "to your props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 330.72,
          "end": 332.46,
          "en": "What's new and important here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 332.46,
          "end": 334.653,
          "en": "is this special children prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.58,
          "end": 338.79,
          "en": "Thus far, we always added our own props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.79,
          "end": 342.24,
          "en": "A post, for example, has our own author and body prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 342.24,
          "end": 344.373,
          "en": "And these names were up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 345.63,
          "end": 347.28,
          "en": "Now, for children, it's different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 349.38,
          "en": "That's a reserved prop name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 349.38,
          "end": 352.59000000000003,
          "en": "because children always refers to the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 352.59000000000003,
          "end": 354.87,
          "en": "that's passed between the opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 354.87,
          "end": 358.473,
          "en": "and closing tags of your custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 359.52,
          "end": 363.57,
          "en": "So here this content, the NewPost component in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 363.57,
          "end": 366.36,
          "en": "that's the value that will be received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 366.36,
          "end": 370.2,
          "en": "on the children prop in this Modal component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 370.2,
          "end": 372.24,
          "en": "And we then output it down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 372.24,
          "end": 375.09,
          "en": "so that we tall React that in the end here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 375.09,
          "end": 377.25,
          "en": "it should output the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 377.25,
          "end": 379.65,
          "en": "that's passed between the modal opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 379.65,
          "end": 381.69,
          "en": "and closing tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 381.69,
          "end": 383.61,
          "en": "Now, with that change applied,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 383.61,
          "end": 386.13,
          "en": "we just have to adjust the styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 386.13,
          "end": 389.88,
          "en": "of this NewPost component here a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 389.88,
          "end": 394.14300000000003,
          "en": "And get rid of this box-shadow, border-radius and margin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 396.06,
          "end": 398.4,
          "en": "And also back in the Modal component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 398.4,
          "end": 403.05,
          "en": "add the special open prop on dialog just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 403.05,
          "end": 405.33,
          "en": "The value theoretically is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 405.33,
          "end": 408,
          "en": "but if you set true as a value for a prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 408,
          "end": 410.7,
          "en": "you can also omit it and just add the prop name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 410.7,
          "end": 414.42,
          "en": "and then true will be used as a default value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 414.42,
          "end": 416.90999999999997,
          "en": "And this open prop is simply required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 416.90999999999997,
          "end": 420.573,
          "en": "by the default dialog element to make sure it's visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 421.53,
          "end": 424.2,
          "en": "And with all these steps taken,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
